.TH "RECORD\-MR\-PROPER\.SH" "" "June 2026" ""
.SH "NAME"
\fBrecord\-mr\-proper\.sh\fR
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBrecord\-mr\-proper\.sh\fR
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fBrecord\-mr\-proper\.sh\fR performs a full reset of the RECORD workflow environment\. It is the RECORD equivalent of \fBmake mrproper\fR in the Linux kernel build system: a destructive, non\-recoverable operation that returns the environment to a clean state\.
.P
The script prompts the user to type \fBYES\fR (uppercase) to confirm intent before proceeding\. Any other input causes the script to exit without taking any action\.
.P
On confirmation the script runs the following steps in order:
.IP "1." 4
\fB\fBrecord\-stop\.sh\fR\fR \(em terminates any running instance of \fBRECORD_START_PROGRAM\fR and removes the PID file\.
.IP "2." 4
\fB\fBrecord\-clean\.sh\fR\fR \(em removes initialisation and output files\.
.IP "3." 4
\fB\fBreccord\-delete\-database\.py\fR\fR \(em deletes the provenance database\.
.IP "4." 4
\fB\fB\. lib\.record\.mrproper\.sh\fR\fR \(em sources any additional project\-specific cleanup defined in \fBlib\.record\.mrproper\.sh\fR\.
.IP "" 0
.SH "OPTIONS"
This script accepts no options or arguments\.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
Returns 0 on successful completion of all steps\.
.P
Returns \-1 (typically 255) if the user does not confirm with \fBYES\fR\.
.P
Returns non\-zero if \fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR validation fails at source time, or if any of the invoked scripts exit with a non\-zero status\.
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
All environment variables required by \fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR, \fBrecord\-stop\.sh\fR, and \fBreccord\-delete\-database\.py\fR are inherited from the calling environment\. Refer to those scripts for the full list\.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
Perform a full reset of the RECORD environment:
.IP "" 4
.nf
export RECORD_START_PROGRAM=my_sim
export RECORD_DBTYPE=sqlite3
record\-mr\-proper\.sh
.fi
.IP "" 0
.SH "FILES"
.TP
\fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR
Common library sourced at startup\. Must be present in the working directory or on \fBPATH\fR\.
.TP
\fBlib\.record\.mrproper\.sh\fR
Project\-specific cleanup library sourced as the final step\. Must be present in the working directory if any project\-specific teardown is required\.
